{
  "question": "Can the same stationary drain supply a weak real trapped wave and remove energy from a stronger one, selecting a physical occupation before a free-fall calculation?",
  "working_base": "1dc45d09de9a8ed1d02337cba71a123d090453f7",
  "preparation": "Prescribed radius-one depth-scale-one cubic profile at rest, unperturbed intake 0.25. Spherical sections in three brane coordinates, with resolved depth w and finite feed/receiving domains. Bath perturbations fixed; AC mass current is allowed to respond. No companion or sideways force.",
  "assumptions": "Real isotropic bound scalar ground mode. A new reciprocal derivative of local squared gap with respect to density around the stored preparation is constant g inside the carrier domain. Its reference well is unchanged. g = +/-1 in model units is a trial response, calibratable by an independent local density/frequency-shift reading. Mode held sinusoidal to compute the first nonzero wave work; the carrier is treated to linear order. Initial scalar energies are .0025 and .01; both measured at the zero-displacement phase. g=0 reproduces the original law.",
  "work": "As the scalar intensity oscillates with a mean and a second harmonic, the carrier sees V=(g E/omega^2) phi(x)^2 sin^2(omega*t). Integral delta n times partial_t V agrees with quadratic carrier energy at each complete cycle. g^2 E^2 scaling is a consequence of this leading-order calculation and does not constrain strong amplitudes. A second script measures signed outward canonical carrier-energy flux toward w<.5 and w>3.05 and independently reconstructs crossings from local energy less work supplied directly in the region.",
  "scope": "No open-bath permanent escape rate, independently measured g or action, amplitude attractor or numerical free-fall acceleration. The fixed-phase preparation has equal reservoir frequencies. No conversion energy reservoir is populated or implicitly credited. Control at zero intake keeps the reference scalar well fixed.",
